### A.3 Proof of Proposition 3.2 (Divergence of Recovery Latency)

**Proposition 3.2.** Under (F1), as \(R \downarrow R_{\text{crit}}\),

\[
\lambda_{\min}(A(R, w)) = \Theta\left(\sqrt{R - R_{\text{crit}}}\right),
\]

provided \(\gamma + \lambda\alpha_\Psi > |m(R)|_-\) and the fold normal form is exact to leading order. Consequently,

\[
\tau_{\text{rec}}(R, w) = \Theta\left((R - R_{\text{crit}})^{-1/2}\right) \to +\infty.
\]

*Proof.* Under (F1), the fast subsystem reduces on a one-dimensional center manifold to \(\dot{C} = a(R - R_{\text{crit}}) + b C^2 + O((R-R_{\text{crit}})^2) + O(C^3)\). The stable equilibrium is \(C^*_{\text{stable}} = -\sqrt{a(R-R_{\text{crit}})/b} + O(R-R_{\text{crit}})\). The curvature of the potential at this equilibrium is

\[
V_{\text{total}}''(C^*_{\text{stable}}) = -2b C^*_{\text{stable}} + O((R-R_{\text{crit}})) = 2\sqrt{ab(R-R_{\text{crit}})} + O(R-R_{\text{crit}}).
\]

The transverse eigenvalues (in directions orthogonal to the center manifold) are bounded away from zero by the normal hyperbolicity assumption. Therefore,

\[
\lambda_{\min}(A(R, w)) = 2\sqrt{ab(R-R_{\text{crit}})} + O(R-R_{\text{crit}}) = \Theta\left(\sqrt{R-R_{\text{crit}}}\right).
\]

The recovery latency is the inverse, giving \(\tau_{\text{rec}} = \Theta((R-R_{\text{crit}})^{-1/2})\). \(\square\)

