### A.9 Proof of Theorem 6.1 (Convergence of Narrative Contestation)

**Theorem 6.1.** Suppose either (H1) the contestation game is a potential game with \(C^2\) potential \(\Phi\) bounded below, or (H2) the game is Rosen-contractive on \(\Delta^{N-1}\). Then the replicator dynamics (6.1) converges to the set of rest points. Under (H1), rest points are Nash equilibria; under (H2), the unique interior rest point is the unique Nash equilibrium.

*Proof.*

**Under (H1).** The replicator equation on the simplex \(\Delta^{N-1}\) is a gradient flow for the potential \(\Phi\) with respect to the Shahshahani metric \(g_{ij} = \delta_{ij}/w_i\). Along trajectories,

\[
\frac{d}{dt}\Phi(w(t)) = \sum_i \frac{\partial \Phi}{\partial w_i}\dot{w}_i = \sum_i \pi_i w_i(\pi_i - \bar{\pi}) = \sum_i w_i(\pi_i - \bar{\pi})^2 \geq 0.
\]

Thus \(\Phi\) is a Lyapunov function. Since \(\Phi\) is bounded below and the simplex is compact, \(\Phi(w(t))\) converges. By LaSalle's invariance principle, \(w(t)\) converges to the largest invariant set contained in \(\{\dot{\Phi} = 0\} = \{\pi_i = \bar{\pi} \text{ for all } i \text{ with } w_i > 0\}\), which is the set of Nash equilibria.

**Under (H2).** The Jacobian of the replicator vector field \(F(w) = (w_i(\pi_i - \bar{\pi}))_i\) on the tangent space of \(\Delta^{N-1}\) is \(J_F = \text{diag}(w) J_\pi (I - \mathbf{1}w^\top) + \text{diag}(\pi - \bar{\pi}\mathbf{1})\). At an interior rest point, \(\pi = \bar{\pi}\mathbf{1}\), so \(J_F = \text{diag}(w) J_\pi (I - \mathbf{1}w^\top)\). Under the Rosen condition, \(J_\pi\) is symmetric negative definite on the tangent space. Since \(\text{diag}(w)\) is positive definite and \(I - \mathbf{1}w^\top\) is a projection onto the tangent space, \(J_F\) is negative definite. By the Hartman–Grobman theorem, the rest point is locally exponentially stable. Global convergence follows from the standard contraction argument with the Lyapunov function \(\|w - w^*\|^2\). \(\square\)

