### A.10 Proof of Proposition 6.1 (Attractor Location)

**Proposition 6.1.** Let \(w^*\) be a rest point of the replicator dynamics. Under the assumptions of Theorem 7.1, the unique minimizer \(C^*(w^*)\) of \(V_{\text{total}}(\cdot; w^*)\) satisfies (6.3), and as \(\lambda \to \infty\), \(C^*(w^*) \to \arg\min_C \Psi(C, R; w^*)\).

*Proof.* The first-order condition for the minimizer is

\[
\nabla_C V_{\text{phys}}(C^*, R) + \gamma C^* + \lambda \sum_i w_i^* \nabla_C \psi_i(C^*, R) = 0,
\]

which is (6.3). Dividing by \(\lambda\) and letting \(\lambda \to \infty\) gives \(\sum_i w_i^* \nabla_C \psi_i(C^*, R) \to 0\), i.e., \(\nabla_C \Psi(C^*, R; w^*) \to 0\). By (N2), \(\Psi\) is convex in \(C\); if \(\alpha_\Psi > 0\), it is strongly convex and the limit is the unique minimizer. If \(\alpha_\Psi = 0\), coercivity (N1) plus strict convexity of \(\Psi\) (assumed) gives uniqueness. \(\square\)

