### A.12 Proof of Corollary 7.1 (Regulatory Coupling)

**Corollary 7.1.** Suppose \(R_t \to R_\infty\) a.s. If \(R_\infty \geq R_{\text{crit}} + \delta\) and (7.1) holds at \(R_\infty\), then \((C_t, R_t) \to (C^*(R_\infty, w^*), R_\infty)\) a.s. If \(R_\infty < R_{\text{crit}}\), the system converges to a ghost-collapse regime.

*Proof.* By Theorem 7.1(iii), for each fixed \(R\), \(C_t\) converges exponentially to \(C^*(R, w^*)\) with rate \(\delta(R)\). By the assumed convergence of \(R_t\) and the continuous dependence of \(C^*\) on \(R\) (Theorem 7.1(iv)), for any \(\eta > 0\) there exists \(T\) such that for \(t \geq T\), \(\|C_t - C^*(R_\infty, w^*)\| \leq \|C_t - C^*(R_t, w^*)\| + \|C^*(R_t, w^*) - C^*(R_\infty, w^*)\| < \eta\). The first term is controlled by the exponential convergence at rate \(\delta(R_t)\) (which is bounded below by \(\delta(R_\infty) > 0\) for \(t\) large), and the second by continuity. The ghost-collapse case follows from Proposition 3.1. \(\square\)

